# U-Boot environment location on the SSC333.
#
# The table below is the one board/sigmastar/post-image.sh generates and the
# one this board is programmed with; mtd0 and mtd1 are fixed by the
# bootloader's compiled CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET/CONFIG_ENV_SIZE, everything after
# them is sized to the built images.
#
#   dev:    size     erasesize  name
#   mtd0: 00040000  00010000  "boot"
#   mtd1: 00010000  00010000  "env"      <- this file
#   mtd2: <sized>   00010000  "kernel"
#   mtd3: <sized>   00010000  "rootfs"
#   mtd4: <rest>    00010000  "data"
#   mtd5: 00800000  00010000  "all"      (8MB, the whole chip at offset 0)
#
# Anything quoting a fixed size for mtd2 onward is quoting one particular
# build. The authority is /proc/mtd on the running unit.
#
# thingino's base overlay/etc/fw_env.config declares a 0x8000 sector, which is
# right for the Ingenic boards it was written for and wrong here: this NOR chip
# erases in 64KB blocks. fw_setenv's write path erases one DEVESIZE chunk at a
# time, so a 0x8000 length reaches MEMERASE unaligned and the ioctl rejects it.
# thingino-sysupgrade (S97sysupgrade) and the WebUI both call fw_setenv, so
# this is a live path, not a theoretical one.
#
# Overridden per-camera rather than by editing the base overlay: Makefile:598
# appends this directory to BR2_ROOTFS_OVERLAY after the shared one, so the
# file here wins with zero merge surface upstream. Promote it to a shared
# SigmaStar overlay if a third board repeats it verbatim -- so far the
# Infinity6E board has the identical file, which is two.
#
# <device> <offset> <env size> <sector size>
/dev/mtd1 0x0 0x10000 0x10000
